; The first three are clean. `2` is `wrong_underlying` (a bare magnitude is
; not a name), and `2.5d` is `not_member` (a real unit-bearing value in a
; slot that accepts them — it just is not one of the three).
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code wrong_underlying :path [texture dimension])
  (diagnostic :code not_member :path [texture dimension]))
